---
title: Pasta alla Nerano
servings: 4
tags: [italian, vegetarian, summer]
cuisine: italian
time: 35 minutes
source: Spaghetti alla Nerano by GialloZafferano, https://www.giallozafferano.com/recipes/Spaghetti-alla-Nerano-spaghetti-with-zucchini.html
---

Trim the @zucchini{700%g} and slice them into thin rounds on a #mandoline{}.

Heat @olive oil{}(extra virgin, for frying) in a #large frying pan{} to 150°C
(300°F). Fry the zucchini in small batches ~{5%minutes} to ~{6%minutes}, until
golden. Lift onto paper towels, salt them, and tear over some of the
@basil{}(leaves).

Put a #tall pot{} of water on to boil and salt it. Coarsely grate the
@provolone{150%g}(Provolone del Monaco, or aged caciocavallo) and the
@parmesan{30%g}(Parmigiano-Reggiano).

Cook the @dried pasta{320%g}(spaghetti) until very al dente, ~{6%minutes}.

In a #wide pan{}, warm the @olive oil{2.5%tbsp}(extra virgin) with the
@garlic{1%clove}(whole), then lift the garlic out. Add the fried zucchini and a
ladle of pasta water and toss briefly to soften them.

Drain the spaghetti into the pan, keeping some of the water. Stir ~{3%minutes},
adding water a little at a time as for risotto, then turn off the heat.

Stir in part of the provolone until it melts into a cream, then the Parmigiano
and the rest of the provolone. Add more torn basil and another ladle of water,
grind over @black pepper{}, and serve hot.
